.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-lsp 1  "lsp " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-lsp \- Run as a Language Server over stdio, for editor integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx lsp\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run as a Language Server over stdio, for editor integration
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `RQX.toml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Leave the mouse to the terminal. Capture takes drag\-select away from it, and not every emulator passes shift+drag through
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

